{"availability":"available","full":"amirhs1/eyvan","name":"eyvan","description":"A Jekyll portfolio theme inspired by the eyvan — an open threshold space in Iranian architecture.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-17T16:11:55Z","updated":"2026-10-11T14:26:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://amirhs1.github.io/eyvan/","topics":["academic-website","github-pages","jekyll","jekyll-theme","markdown","personal-website","portfolio-website","theme"],"demo":"https://amirhs1.github.io/eyvan/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:10.526Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:10.526Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:10.526Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:05:10.526Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Eyvan — marked by the A1 logo (pronounced /ey-van/) — is a visually minimalist, feature-rich Jekyll template inspired by the eyvan or ayvan, an open threshold space in Iranian architecture.","The template is designed for personal portfolios, academic profiles, research notes, project archives, and long-form technical writing. Its interface is restrained, but the template includes a complete publishing system: layouts, reusable Liquid includes, Sass architecture, JavaScript interactions, tag archives, social sharing, MathJax, media figures, and GitHub Actions deployment."],"features":["Responsive, content-first layouts for phones, tablets, and desktop screens","Light/dark theme toggle with early theme initialization","Homepage hero driven by data/hero.yml and data/author.yml","A deliberately unified content model: posts serve as both writing and project","entries, with a Projects archive and tag pages instead of a separate collection"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amirhs1/eyvan/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f295c6837d931f805ac08bc63c5d8fe269bccaaa23ae439fa5f5e1ae04ecc8f5","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:10.656Z"},"overv